  "id": "s01-pushback-tug-contact",
  "title": "Towbar shear and nose-gear contact on pushback",
  "narrative": "Manchester, early departure bank. Accent Air ACX211 to Palma, an A320 (AX-MAB) with 174 passengers, is being pushed back from stand 32 when the towbar shear pin fails. The tug brakes, rolls on and makes contact with the nose landing gear before the aircraft stops just clear of the stand. No one is hurt. The captain sets the parking brake, shuts down and asks for engineering. The aircraft has three more sectors today (Palma back to Manchester, then a Dublin return). A spare A320 is due to finish a check at minute 50. The handler is short of tugs this morning.",
  "visibility": "public",
  "inspiredBy": [
    {
      "sourceId": "AAIB Airbus A320-214, G-EZTV",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/aaib-reports/aaib-investigation-to-airbus-a320-214-g-eztv",
      "note": "Towbar shear pins fractured during pushback at Manchester and the tug then struck the aircraft (UK AAIB report)."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "ASRS ACN 1577181",
